# entity_serde — every bug this target has found, pinned forever.
# One decimal master seed per line; `--seed <n>` reproduces one exactly.

# ── createEntity threw on a wrong-typed field ────────────────────────────────
# nlohmann's `value()` does not fall back to the default when the key exists
# with the wrong type — it throws. scene_serializer.h wraps only json::parse in
# try/catch, so one `"fov": "60"` in a hand-edited .scene propagated out of
# scene load and took down the editor or the player. Roughly 1 case in 20.
2277151743773813066
12660276661850738527
2267135806626478818
8704601960889612507
3600414414911528964
1004782555136890424

# ── SEGFAULT: short float array, const operator[] out of range ───────────────
# `j["halfExtent"][0..2]` on a two-element array. nlohmann's CONST
# operator[](size_type) is undefined behaviour out of range — not at(), no
# bounds check, no exception. Five sites had it (position, rotation, scale,
# clearColor, halfExtent, color). Reproduced as a null-json deref with an
# unwindable-stack crash. Only reachable AFTER the type-tolerance fix above,
# because until then the wrong-type throw got there first.
5813135465557942230

# ── Non-finite values accepted ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# JSON has no NaN literal, but `1e999` parses to +inf, and an infinite scale or
# fov propagates into every world matrix and projection downstream — corrupting
# a frame far from the load that caused it.
1363229889033388563
3343848946614325241
